1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,600
Five years never guaranteed settlement.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:07,300
It meant we could apply — if we met the requirements.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,900
We already had to meet residence, salary, sponsorship and suitability rules,

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:16,800
and demonstrate English and knowledge of life in the UK.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,600
Now, many existing migrants face a longer pathway,

6
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:28,400
after building their careers and family plans around the published rules.

7
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:38,600
The Migration Advisory Committee estimated a positive lifetime fiscal contribution for general Skilled Worker main applicants.

8
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:44,500
That is a modelled cohort average. Not a promise about every person.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,000
The real question is what changes when the same people must wait another five years.

10
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,900
That needs evidence on earnings, public spending, job mobility and people leaving.

11
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,000
Publish the full impact assessment.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,800
Explain the alternatives.

13
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:08,200
Give everyone already on a five-year route fair transitional protection.

14
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,400
We followed the rules.

15
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:14,000
Let us complete the pathway.
